  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="77a7-f2ae-588c-7af2" name="Han Chinese (AoA2) - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF ANTIQUITY v2 #35 (unofficial, Martin Gibbins). The Han came to power in a rebellion against Qin rule. The dynasty provided a series of more popular rulers and was to last four hundred years. Initially it was necessary to deal with the Xiongnu, after which Han emperors extended Chinese rule to nearer Korea, the southern jungles and into Ferghana to the west, from which trade routes would lead to the Middle East and Rome. Han China was divided into a series of military districts and use was made of conscription to create large armies at need. Allies: The army may have allies from the Xiongnu list.

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Han Chinese]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Chariotry and Cavalry: at least 25%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  Characters: up to 25% Chariotry and Cavalry: At least 25% Infantry: At least 25% Artillery: up to 110 points Allies: Up to 25%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
